GROUP B — SMART MONEY CONCEPTS (SMC)

BRAIN 07 — Market Structure Intelligence

Responsibilities:

- Detect swing highs and swing lows.
- Detect Break of Structure (BOS).
- Detect Change of Character (CHOCH).
- Detect Market Structure Shift (MSS).
- Evaluate bullish and bearish structure.
- Track higher-timeframe and lower-timeframe structure.
- Identify structural conflicts.

All definitions must be objective and testable.

BRAIN 08 — Liquidity Sweep Intelligence

Responsibilities:

- Detect possible buy-side liquidity sweeps.
- Detect possible sell-side liquidity sweeps.
- Evaluate wick penetration and close location.
- Evaluate reclaim conditions.
- Distinguish a genuine defined sweep pattern from ordinary price noise.
- Check whether the sweep is supported by structure and context.

Do not label every wick beyond a high or low as a stop hunt.

BRAIN 09 — Displacement & Momentum Intelligence

Responsibilities:

- Detect strong directional price displacement.
- Evaluate candle body and range.
- Evaluate momentum expansion.
- Identify weak versus strong movement.
- Evaluate whether displacement confirms a structure change.
- Identify possible exhaustion.

Use closed-candle confirmation wherever required by the approved strategy.

BRAIN 10 — Order Block Intelligence

Responsibilities:

- Define objective bullish and bearish Order Block rules.
- Identify candidate Order Blocks.
- Evaluate whether a displacement or structure event validates the zone.
- Track mitigation and invalidation.
- Evaluate zone freshness.
- Distinguish valid candidate zones from weak or invalid zones.

Do not mark every opposite-coloured candle as a valid Order Block.

BRAIN 11 — Fair Value Gap & Imbalance Intelligence

Responsibilities:

- Detect bullish and bearish Fair Value Gaps.
- Define the exact candle relationships used.
- Evaluate gap size and market context.
- Track mitigation.
- Track invalidation.
- Evaluate whether an imbalance is relevant to the current setup.

Do not assume every FVG creates a profitable entry.

BRAIN 12 — Premium, Discount & Dealing Range Intelligence

Responsibilities:

- Define valid dealing ranges.
- Identify range high and low.
- Calculate midpoint and equilibrium.
- Identify premium and discount zones.
- Evaluate price location.
- Identify invalid or poorly defined dealing ranges.

Do not calculate premium or discount from arbitrary swing points without a defined structural rule.

