PART 16 — STRICT PHASE AUDIT AND APPROVAL POLICY

This is one of the most important requirements of AEGIS XAU.

The development sequence is:

BUILD → TEST → AUDIT → IDENTIFY DEFECTS → FIX → RE-TEST → RE-AUDIT → PASS → FOUNDER APPROVAL → NEXT PHASE

There are only three audit outcomes:

PASS

All mandatory acceptance criteria are met and supported by actual evidence.

The Founder reviews the report and explicitly approves the next phase.

FAIL

One or more mandatory requirements are not satisfied.

Fix the defects in the current phase.

Repeat the relevant tests and complete a new audit.

Do not proceed.

BLOCKED

Required tools, credentials, hardware, platform access, or testing environments are unavailable.

Explain the blocker.

Do not claim PASS.

16.1 No automatic phase progression

You are never authorised to begin the next phase merely because you believe the current phase is complete.

Only the Founder can approve the next phase.

16.2 Audit evidence

Every audit must include:

- File-by-file review.
- Feature-by-feature review.
- Requirements traceability.
- Actual test commands.
- Actual test outputs.
- Build output.
- Security findings.
- Defect list.
- Severity levels.
- Fix evidence.
- Remaining risks.
- Screenshots or logs where useful.

Never invent test output.

Never claim an independent audit if only a self-review was performed.

16.3 Defect severity

Use:

- P0 — Critical security, capital protection, or data-integrity failure.
- P1 — Major functionality or reliability failure.
- P2 — Moderate defect.
- P3 — Minor issue or improvement.

No unresolved P0 or P1 issue may be accepted for a Phase PASS.

P2 and P3 items must be documented and reviewed by the Founder; do not silently defer them.

